# Wave W17-X (Route 210): paddock post — a paddock marker post at the north fence, the herd’s fence: a thick weathered post carrying two short rail stubs at mid height, the fence line’s grammar kept in a single standing piece (design: the herd bunched flame-maned at the north fence like the road owes them a race — the posts stand where the fence turns the herd). On ranch turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s posts by the rail stubs entire: bands and caps mark and measure, this post fences.
